A||N||48||DISenchanted||Macintosh or Windows?||||5||
Z||000000||DISenchanted||04-10-2001||05:08 AM||||I just read the thread on Windows ME, and wondered if anyone else out there was on a Macintosh.  I got sick of Windows' crap and bought a Mac.  I must say it was the best investment I ever made (aside from my fiero's).  I just wanted to know what everyone else was using for a computer.<P>DISenchanted||||reg||5
Z||000001||Songman||04-10-2001||09:00 AM||||I've got a PC now, IBM Aptiva to be exact. I started buying PCs after I left the corporate world because I had to start spending my own money!<P>Prior to that I spent 10 years in the advertising and graphic design business for a Fortune 200 company down in GA. Of course, we used Macs. <P>I have always, and still do, love Mac computers. Just coincidentally, my corporate life started along the same time Apple Computer released the new amazing computer! It still amazes me that for years I used a Mac II with 8 megs of RAM and a 40 meg HD to do advertising for such a huge company. When I left there, I had a Quadra 950 that I was able to get a PowerPC upgrade card for before they had been released. Sadly, the card didn't work all that well. <P>Counting output devices, I had about $80,000 worth of computer sitting on my desk when I left there in the early 90s. My $1500 IBM can run circles around that baby now! Not because PCs are better, just years of technological advances.<P>The last Mac I owned was a PowerMac 2600. Wish I could afford to have a new G4 right now, but I would want it sitting right bere by my PC. They are both great machines.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Raydar||04-10-2001||09:26 AM||||It's what you're accustomed to...<BR>My wife used to have a Mac. A Performa something-or-other. She loved it. I knew absolutely nothing about it.<BR>We both have PCs now, since that is what we both use at work. She's got a Dell Optiplex, since she needs a reliable system, and I've got a dual-Celeron box that I cobbled together, so that I can "play". <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> Since I did PC support at work (until I ran screaming from the department in November), supporting our systems is not a big deal.<BR>I do believe that Macs make the best computers for graphic artists, though. <BR>Just an observation. Not the voice of experience.<P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<P>88 T-top Formula<BR>88 soon-to-be-V6 coupe||||reg||1
Z||000003||JSocha||04-10-2001||09:34 AM||||PC - Nothing more...nothing less  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Mac?  Isn't that what McDonald's sells?  Big Mac's?  They aren't as good either!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif"><P>Your MAC may be surviving now, but that is thanks inpart to MicroSoft as they now own Apple (at least last time I had heard).<P>Sometime, someplace, you could be soooorrrrryyyy, 'cause I feel BG will eventually get tired of selling a "Pepsi" with every six pack of Coke (or vice versa however he stated that during his Monopoly hearing) and he'll ditch the product and sell only a six pack of Coke (I prefer Pepsi myself).<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fiero5a_3.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||TheFiero64||04-10-2001||10:45 AM||||I am a PC kind of guy. <P>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://people.ne.mediaone.net/fiero64/Fiero642.jpg"> <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>||||reg||1
Z||000005||Tigger||04-10-2001||12:31 PM||||I have a really old Mac from '84.  It's funny how much it looks A LOT like a Windows system.  Hmmmm....||||reg||3
Z||000006||Songman||04-10-2001||12:35 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Raydar:<BR><B>I do believe that Macs make the best computers for graphic artists, though. <BR>Just an observation. Not the voice of experience.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>I do have the voice of experience. And you are exactly right. If I were still doing graphic design I would still be using a Mac. The PC has come a long way, but the Mac still has the edge.<P>One place where this gets fuzzy is graphic design for the web.. PC has the edge here.<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by JSocha:<BR><B>Your MAC may be surviving now, but that is thanks inpart to MicroSoft as they now own Apple (at least last time I had heard).<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Don't know where you heard this tidbit but it is not true. Apple Computers had their low times but they are not owned by Microsoft. There were some joint venture things going on, like the PowerPC chip, but they were never followed to completion.<P>Ten years ago we were all saying that in ten years we would have cross-platform computing where even though each type was different, there would be enough instruction sets so that the same piece of software would work on either one... from what I have seen, that is no closer than it was ten years ago and they don't want it to get that way. And I don't think w do either. We like having our little Mac vs. PC discussions.<P>Truth is that they are both great computers.<BR><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
Z||000007||Songman||04-10-2001||12:38 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Tigger:<BR><B>I have a really old Mac from '84.  It's funny how much it looks A LOT like a Windows system.  Hmmmm....</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Actually, it is funny how much the Windows system looks like the old Mac system. The Mac came first...<P>And to be even funnier, you have to look how much that first Mac looks like another GUI system that was developed before that. Steve Jobs stole the technology and changed it to work on his new Mac computers...<P>Who was this company that created the basis for all of our GUI computers?<P>Of all people... XEROX. They were the first ones.. <P><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
Z||000008||Songman||04-10-2001||12:43 PM||||Sorry! One more...<P>Wanna see what the guy who actually 'invented' the Apple computer is doing now? No, not the guy who took credit for it..<P>Steve Wozniak was the brains behind Apple Computers. Steve Jobs was the mouthpiece.<P>Woz is now spending his life doing all sorts of cool things that are actually good for people. He tries to help.<P>I actually had quite a long string of e-mail conversations with him. He has an e-mail address there. Write to him, he will write back.<P> <A HREF="http://www.woz.org" TARGET=_blank>http://www.woz.org</A> <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
Z||000009||btoth||04-10-2001||02:26 PM||||Each system has their pros and cons.  I like the Mac OS over anything Microsoft, but Apple rips you off for their systems (my opinion).  I've owned two Macs and now my PC so I've used them both and would really like a G4 execpt that they're so darned expensive.<P>MacOS X is very cool.  I was reading somewhere that Intel is developing their 64bit processors (G4's are 128bit) but I guess their having a hard time making Windows work with the 64bit achitecture.  If I were in charge of Apple (dreaming here  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">) I would port MacOS X to the PC and compete with windows.  ||||reg||1
Z||000010||ray b||04-10-2001||03:57 PM||||my mac is a power PC #6205 performa.<BR>it slow as hell for internet use, any cheap way to speed it up? with dial 56k modum.<BR>what kind of M sims does it use?<BR>it is just a 2nd computer as kids on main one most of time.||||reg||1
Z||000011||JSocha||04-10-2001||04:01 PM||||Songman,<P>I know back sometime around 1997/98, Steve Jobs took over again as Apple's CEO (?) to get them back out of the hole.  Don't know if he is still on the Board today, as again I do not keep up with Apple news.<P>I had heard that Microsoft had purchased a large portion of Apple's stock and subsequently had become the controlling interest in Apple Computers.  It was either reported on "The Screen Savers, Silicon Spin, Internet Tonight or other show that was running on ZDTV (nka:  TechTV)" back last summer/fall and before the wife and I moved into our new house in November.<P>Also, since then, a computer salesman out of Minot who has been trying to gain our business for years now, has come in repeatedly and talked about Microsoft owning Apple Computers and that the Apple Computer division would eventually be dissolved if Microsoft didn't make a profit and just gather Apple's technology (especially after the release of the G4 as Microsoft wanted to see if this would help the division survive before make a final decision to disolve the division - G4 piece of junk if you ask me).<P>Since then, I guess I have taken what I had heard and what the salesman spoke about as fact and not as a possible "rumor".<P>So, if I was wrong (as obviously I am not perfect - even though I like to think so from time to time) in my previous statement (and my understanding these past months  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/redface.gif">), let it be known that I have been corrected and to ignore any of my previous statement about Microsoft owning Apple.<P>Later...and Songman...Thank you for setting me straight on the "true facts!".<P>Appreciate it!  Now I won't sound like a potential idiot (as I did here) in the future should I discuss this topic with anyone else, now that clarification on this subject has been made.<P>Learn something new everyday...!<P>Later Songman!<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fiero5a_3.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000012||Raydar||04-10-2001||04:12 PM||||To further inflame the thread...<P>AMIGA!<BR>One of the ultimate "hobby" computers. Have only ever seen one. Never drove one. Have read a little bit about them. All the true "chipheads" that I know still salivate at the mere mention of the name.<P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<P>88 T-top Formula<BR>88 soon-to-be-V6 coupe||||reg||1
Z||000013||fierogt88||04-10-2001||04:23 PM||||You were not incorrect.  Bill Gates has controlling interest in Apple.  I am not sure whether it is through microsoft or whether it is Bill himself, but Bill is the top dog there now.  I program industrial software and talk to Microsoft reps all the time.  The advantage that the Mac's had in the graphics department was from specializatoin, not because it was a better machine.  I know how to program on both platforms and i can tell you that there is very little perfomance difference between the two, once you start comparing apples to apples... err umm  you know what i mean.  For the same dollars a PC will do everything the Mac can do, and except for in the very beginning, always could.  The reason everyone seems to like the Mac better for graphics opps is because Apple has always wined and dined the graphics software companies, so they developed the software for that platform.<P>Of course, that specialization has also been the drawback of Macs (and the horred one-button mouse... ).<P>If you really did your research, historically Alphas and Silicon Graphics systems whooped everybody's arse in the graphics arena.  And without the corner on graphics there isn't much left to justify a Mac.<P>PC for me.  All around powerhouses and best bang for the buck.  Sadly, most of my experience has been on Sun systems.  I hate em.  Everybody I ever worked for thinks they are "god's gift to technology" but trust me, they're crap.||||reg||1
Z||000014||JSocha||04-10-2001||04:42 PM||||FIEROGT88,<P>I'll split the difference at this point who owns/or does not own what.  Like it will really matter as it seems to me MS is driving the computer industry one way or the other and the people who own computers nuts with all the MS OS crashes.<P>Since you "PROGRAM" though, do you have any leads on any individuals looking for a "programming" job in ND?   Rugby Mfg. Co. (http://www.rugbymfg.com) was looking several months back for a programmer and we found one.  <P>However, I would like to have other qualified individuals apply if they are seeking a programming job to see if maybe their qualifications may meet future objectives for our company.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fiero5a_3.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000015||DISenchanted||04-10-2001||05:10 PM||||Bill Gates doesn't have a controlling interest in Apple.  A while back, Microsoft gave Apple $500 Million to license technology.  Other then that, Bill can't have a controlling interest in Apple.  Apple is one of the only reasons he does not have a Monopoly.<P>Glad to see so many responses, sorry it appears that I am the only "Mac" user at this point...<P>It is a Beautiful Machine, My 400mhz G4 laptop.  Plus it skates circles around even the new 1ghz Pentium laptops.  I will agree though, Apple hardware is really over priced.  But I guess that you get what you pay for.<P>ray b: As far as your Performa, there are no major upgrades available for it.  You might want to try penny-saver.  I saw a few iMac's for under $300.  That should be a substantial upgrade.||||reg||5
